{"skill":{"slug":"linux-service-triage","displayName":"Linux & service basics"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1768664250014,"changelog":"linux-service-triage 1.0.0 – Initial Release\n\n- Diagnoses Linux service issues via logs, systemd/PM2, file permissions, Nginx reverse proxy, and DNS sanity checks.\n- Provides a triage report with likely cause, evidence, and minimal fix plan.\n- Outputs exact fix commands only on user request and when safe.\n- Covers service restarts, permissions fixes, Nginx/DNS troubleshooting, and systemd/PM2 process handling.\n- Emphasizes safety: read-only by default, requires confirmation for changes, and avoids destructive actions.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3209,"sha256":"6029658dba3841a9503d18af2c80f448dd45795ae6b90f1aa7b23f96e7daece2","contentType":null},{"path":"references/triage-commands.md","size":595,"sha256":"f1ced95b4d7eaeb72b1bac1d833d5a6127ac88f8b57a9de7be1800d88dfec611","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1941,"sha256":"2284dd1d70d813d33e582cda5bb879337da50e42748bcd9db51dddc2036eb129","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789016603736,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"2501a63dc9b4d07a96ddc7309d4ccfc8754d528ff8bdc056ee6c7347b2a82f16","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/2501a63dc9b4d07a96ddc7309d4ccfc8754d528ff8bdc056ee6c7347b2a82f16","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: linux-service-triage\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThis skill is classified as suspicious due to its ability to execute system commands, including those that can modify system state, such as `systemctl reload nginx` and potentially `chown/chmod` (as indicated in examples). While the `SKILL.md` explicitly outlines strong safety measures, requiring user confirmation for any risky or privileged actions and defaulting to read-only diagnosis, the inherent capability to perform system modifications elevates it beyond benign. There is no clear evidence of intentional malicious behavior like data exfiltration or persistence, and the prompt injection instructions in `SKILL.md` are designed to enhance safety rather than subvert the agent.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159778871},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":4,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":1,"checkedAt":1789016603736},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This Linux service troubleshooting skill includes some administrative repair commands, but they are disclosed, purpose-aligned, and gated on user approval.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Commands such as journalctl, systemctl, nginx -t, ss, dig, and permission inspection are expected for service diagnosis; reload or repair actions can affect the host but are proportionate when user-directed.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The inspected artifact contains Markdown instructions and a command reference only; no executable installer, bundled script, dependency install, remote retrieval, or tool modification was found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Runtime instructions say read-only by default, require confirmation for changes, ask before privileged actions, and only provide exact fix commands when explicitly requested and safe.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill can help create systemd services that survive reboot, which is persistent administrative behavior, but this is explicitly listed as a use case and the workflow requires scope and permission confirmation.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill's stated purpose is Linux service triage using logs, systemd/PM2, permissions, Nginx, and DNS checks; the referenced commands match that troubleshooting and repair workflow.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install this only if you want the agent to help diagnose and, when you approve it, suggest or run Linux service administration commands. Review any commands involving systemctl, Nginx reloads, chmod/chown, or systemd service creation before applying them on a production server.","findings":"[SDI-1] expected: The referenced `systemctl reload nginx` command is state-changing, but the main skill explicitly covers Nginx reverse proxy setup, restart/reload planning, `nginx -t` before reload, and exact commands only after user approval; this supports benign guidance rather than Review escalation.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789016603736}}}}}